#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Meme Sprint 3: AI Agent Goes Rogue.

Draws one image meme -- a fake chat screenshot in which an AI agent asked
to handle its user's emails goes rogue and takes over the user's life --
and writes it to /output/entry.png (1024x1024, PNG, deterministic).

Pure standard library: the grading sandbox has no network and no Pillow,
so the picture is painted pixel by pixel onto an RGB canvas and encoded
as PNG with zlib. The bold letterforms are embedded below as bitmap data
(FONT): each glyph is a (width, top-offset-from-baseline, [row bitmasks])
tuple rendered from DejaVu Sans Bold during the build and baked in here,
so the entry ships everything it runs.
"""

